{"name":"Post Apocalyptic Cloud","hex":"#c8cdd8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"post","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long dowel or plank protruding from the ground; a fencepost; a lightpost.","A pole erected to mark a spot."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hang (a notice) in a conspicuous manner for general review.","To announce publicly; to publish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/post"},{"term":"apocalyptic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to an apocalypse:\n Revelatory; prophetic.\n\n Catastrophic; disastrous.","Revelatory; prophetic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who predicts apocalypse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apocalyptic"},{"term":"cloud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A visible mass of water droplets suspended in the air.","Any mass of dust, steam or smoke resembling such a mass."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become foggy or gloomy, or obscured from sight.","To overspread or hide with a cloud or clouds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apocalyptic and post-apocalyptic fiction","blocks":[{"text":"Apocalyptic and post-apocalyptic fiction are subgenres of speculative fiction in which the Earth's civilization is collapsing or has collapsed. The apocalypse event may be climatic, such as runaway climate change; astronomical, an impact event; destructive, nuclear holocaust or resource depletion; medical, a pandemic, whether natural or human-caused; end time, such as the Last Judgment, Second Coming, 2012 Phenomenon or Ragnarök; or any other scenario in which the outcome is apocalyptic, such as a zombie apocalypse, AI takeover, technological singularity, dysgenics/eugenics, natural disasters, or alien invasions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Apocalypse-Albert_Goodwin.jpg/330px-Apocalypse-Albert_Goodwin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apocalyptic_and_post-apocalyptic_fiction","wikidata":"Q197949"},{"title":"Cloud","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, a cloud is an aerosol consisting of a visible mass of miniature liquid droplets, ice crystals, or other particles, suspended in the atmosphere of a planetary body or similar space. Water, primarily, comprises the droplets and crystals. On Earth, clouds are formed as a result of saturation of the air when it is cooled to its dew point, or when it gains sufficient moisture, usually in the form of water vapor, from an adjacent source to raise the dew point to the ambient temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg/330px-ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud","wikidata":"Q8074"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Imagination_195403.jpg/330px-Imagination_195403.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Imagination_195403.jpg/330px-Imagination_195403.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Imagination magazine cover, depicting an atomic explosion, dated March 1954","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImagination_195403.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/The_Stand_%281978%29_front_cover%2C_first_edition.png/500px-The_Stand_%281978%29_front_cover%2C_first_edition.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/The_Stand_%281978%29_front_cover%2C_first_edition.png/500px-The_Stand_%281978%29_front_cover%2C_first_edition.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c